1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,220
For many white-collar workers around the world, the recent pandemic has meant having to work from home.
对于全球许多白领员工而言，近年来的疫情意味着他们不得不居家办公。

2
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:12,530
Their usual office location has been out of bounds.
他们平日里的办公地点已经禁止入内。

3
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:20,430
This means different working practices, which have advantages and disadvantages for employees.
这意味着迥然不同的工作模式，对员工而言各有利弊。

4
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:26,140
But the big question is, will they ever see their offices again?
但一个关键问题是：他们还会重返办公室吗？

5
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:36,530
Home working has made people realise what tasks they can perform at home, rather than enduring a commute to the office to do the same thing.
居家办公让人们意识到，有些工作完全可以在家完成，不必忍受通勤之苦跑去办公室做同样的事。

6
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:46,200
It has given them more time with the family; they’ve been sleeping better and have saved money by not travelling or buying lunches on the go.
居家办公让他们有了更多陪伴家人的时间，睡眠质量也有所提升，同时还省下了通勤费用和外出买午餐的开支。

7
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:53,560
And recent research suggests the majority of people working from home are just as productive.
近期研究表明，大多数居家办公的人，工作效率和在办公室时不相上下。

8
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:57,760
For some people, this could be a permanent arrangement.
对有些人来说，居家办公可能会成为一种长期安排。

9
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:09,820
In the UK, fifty of the biggest employers questioned by the BBC, have said they have no plans to return all staff to the office full-time in the near future.
在英国，英国广播公司调查的五十家大型企业均表示，近期不打算让所有员工全职返回办公室办公。

10
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:21,480
Of course, one main reason is that firms couldn’t see a way of accommodating large numbers of staff while social distancing regulations were still in place.
当然，一个主要原因是，在社交距离规定仍然生效的情况下，企业无法找到合适的办法来容纳大量员工办公。

11
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:29,530
But the BBC also heard from some smaller businesses who are deciding to abandon their offices altogether.
但英国广播公司也了解到，一些小型企业正决定彻底放弃办公场所。

12
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:38,220
Other bigger companies are also looking at shutting offices to save money as many jobs can be performed remotely.
其他大型企业也在考虑关闭办公场所来节省开支，因为许多工作都可以远程完成。

13
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:51,740
Peter Cheese, head of the Chartered Institute of Personnel and Development, told the BBC: “We’re at a moment of real change in the world of work, driven by big existential crises.”
英国特许人事与发展协会负责人彼得·奇斯向英国广播公司表示：“在重大生存危机的推动下，我们正处于职场发生真正变革的时刻。”

14
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:55,900
But this isn’t great news for everyone.
但这对所有人而言并非都是好消息。

15
00:01:55,900 --> 00:02:06,610
Some employees can feel isolated at home, and there’s less opportunity to network or learn from other people, especially if they’re a new recruit.
有些员工在家办公会感到孤立无援，而且建立人脉或向他人学习的机会也会减少，新员工尤其如此。

16
00:02:06,610 --> 00:02:12,540
Also, city centres may suffer most from a change in working habits.
此外，工作习惯的改变可能会对市中心造成最严重的冲击。

17
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:20,010
Shops and cafes rely on the footfall of office workers, and without them, they face closure.
商店和咖啡馆都依赖白领员工带来的客流量，失去了这些客源，它们就面临着倒闭的风险。

18
00:02:20,010 --> 00:02:28,490
The future is still uncertain, which is why it may be too early to say where our desks will be permanently located.
未来仍充满不确定性，因此现在断言我们的办公桌会长期放置在何处还为时过早。

19
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:32,720
But the office of the future may be your home.
但未来的办公室，或许就是你的家。
